at's the things going to come up it  can be incredibly distracting so as long  as you're not harming anyone else's  chances don't give a crap about anybody  else on what they're doing just do what  you need to do to do your best you can  be incredibly selfish just before you go  to exam like I said it's always not  harming anyone else's chances do what  you need to do and that can be sitting  in the corner reading through notes it  can be meditating it can be talking to  your friends just make sure that you are  doing what you want to do don't feel  pressured into doing something else it's  really the most important time arguably  just we go to the exam to really make  sure your blade is as sharp as possible  your mind as a sharp as possible and you  are going to do your absolute best so  that's what I have to say on exam  technique if you missed the video last  week I did one on exam preparation and  revision and hopefully by this point you  are really in the run of doing past  papers and you are getting yourself  ready for your exams all I can say is  best of luck to everybody who's doing  them and next week they'll just be a  quick video from me providing hopefully  a little bit of motivation and  encouraging you to keep pushing right to  the end thanks very much for watching  and if you found this video useful then  consider giving it a like or subscribe  to the channel and the very best of luck  with your exams

